  {
    "sha": "750a7c0d97bb01c1bdf126fd6bf5722da17e8998",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOAPHdINoAKDc1MGE3YzBkOTdiYjAxYzFiZGYxMjZmZDZiZjU3MjJkYTE3ZTg5OTg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "IceLocke",
        "email": "lockeice@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-02T05:00:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Jakob Unterwurzacher",
        "email": "jakobunt@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-17T20:30:10Z"
      },
      "message": "kill: option for triggering kernel oom killer\n\nAs mentioned in issue\nhttps://github.com/rfjakob/earlyoom/issues/358 and README, after\nLinux 5.17, OOM sysrq will always kill a process.\n\nThis implements an option for trigger the kernel oom killer i.e.\nwrite an `f` to `/proc/sysrq-trigger`. Since the victim cannot be\nchosen by earlyoom, some of the features about customized victim\nselection won't take effect.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "d8363214aee38f53a32ffef73919511b03c6e492",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rfjakob/earlyoom/git/trees/d8363214aee38f53a32ffef73919511b03c6e492"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rfjakob/earlyoom/git/commits/750a7c0d97bb01c1bdf126fd6bf5722da17e8998",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
