  },
  {
    "sha": "42860d6cc149868e087c106eb894a5274bf17212",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOAPHdINoAKDQyODYwZDZjYzE0OTg2OGUwODdjMTA2ZWI4OTRhNTI3NGJmMTcyMTI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Jakob Unterwurzacher",
        "email": "jakobunt@gmail.com",
        "date": "2022-11-12T19:27:23Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Jakob Unterwurzacher",
        "email": "jakobunt@gmail.com",
        "date": "2022-11-12T19:27:23Z"
      },
      "message": "Don't kill anything if there's not enough anon memory used\n\nWhen /dev/shm and /tmp (when on tmpfs) gets filled up, earlyoom\nwould start killing everything, without improving the situation.\n\nCheck if we *possibly* could kill enough processes (i.e. anon memory)\nto get the available memory over the minimum. If not, do nothing.\n\nFixes: https://github.com/rfjakob/earlyoom/pull/274\nFixes: https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1012870",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "df13adb177d84954090d5f0d4be6ea503d0e08ac",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rfjakob/earlyoom/git/trees/df13adb177d84954090d5f0d4be6ea503d0e08ac"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/rfjakob/earlyoom/git/commits/42860d6cc149868e087c106eb894a5274bf17212",
